<p>Salutations one and all,<br />
I go by JoysticKnight (I imagine you could shorten that to Jsk if it's a little much to type out).</p>
<p>I tend to be an avid enthusiast of design. I like to break apart the inner workings of all this world has to offer. Be it science, psychology, philosophy, art, traditional/video-games, or music to name a few large topics. Although, I do have a particular affinity towards music analysis, and game design.</p>
<p>As far as the foundation is concerned, I've seen it's growth over the years with the wealth of it's library and the troves of content people make concerning it. I indeed have adored the vast imagination of it's machinations showing thoroughly no true limit to the vastness of this world. And it's by this merit I have finally grown enough gall to even consider joining.</p>
<p>Personally speaking I tend to be a shelled and hermit-like in nature. So forgive me if it takes some time to flourish in any way. I have something of a social life, but tend to not act upon it, so participating in a forum or collective source is a rather new experience for me.</p>
<p>I hope that as time marches on I am able to contribute in some forward manner, gaining people's trust and flame of curiousity. Until then, I am but still just another peer.</p>
<p>Also I obvisouly don't talk with this much grandure in real life, it's just nice every once in a while to really convey the right emotions with fitting words.</p>
<p>So about that question. I suppose I'll go with water, it's an endlessly malleable substance that we learn does something new every 5 years or so. I admire it's ability to function and create function.</p>

							</div>

								
					
