														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4823036">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes.</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article.</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> The Painter is a humanoid male with little to no facial features except his eyes, he is able to decide the (<span style="text-decoration: underline;">horrible and gruesome</span>) fate of any living being by painting it on a canvas, no matter how hard his victims will try they will always meet their fate, this manipulates the world around the victim so that they will meet their fate no matter the cost, <span style="text-decoration: underline;">his only limitation is that he must know how the victim looks like in order to put them on the canvas and decide their fate</span>. The foundation is unable to take the paintbrush and the canvas of the Painter because his own fate is to keep painting, so any attempt in doing so will be an inevitable failure because a series of events will always happen in order for the SCP to get his tools back.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> The Painter's story is that he is the judge of humanity, he is here to create and manipulate everyone's fate, he decides how and when everyone will experience their final moments and he will not stop until everyone's fate is set.</p>
<p>He was originally found in a cabin in the woods after a few campers reported &quot;A weird man painting me and my friends dying in horrible ways&quot;. After a few years all of the campers died exactly how they reported the paintings to look like and that's when the foundation stepped in, they used smoke grenades, thermal vision and a bag to blind the target and capture it but being captured by the foundation was only part of his fate.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> The article will contain a few victims of the Painter and how they met their grim fate, how the foundation will try and stop the painter from continuing his anomalous activities and the effect he had on the world around him and the foundation by deciding people's fate.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> This is an old idea, my first one actually, I made an old thread about it almost a year ago and I'm trying to revisit the concept and improve it. hopefully I will be able to achieve that, if you decide to visit the old thread and find that you like the original concept more or some ideas from it, just let me know.</p>

							</div>

								
					
